<%# Lab page for the Phantom MOBILE deep link.

    TWO STATES ON ONE PAGE, chosen by the deeplink query parameter, because the
    property under test is a DIFFERENCE. The gem's wallet picker gates its mobile
    Phantom row on a bare typeof startPhantomDeepLink test, so the entry point must
    be ABSENT when the partial is not rendered and PRESENT when it is. Both states
    ship byte-identical picker markup, so only a browser can tell them apart. A page
    that could render one state could not observe that difference at all.

    NOTHING HERE REIMPLEMENTS THE DEEP LINK. The browser program lives in the gem
    partial solana_studio/phantom_deeplink and is rendered BY NAME below. A lab page
    that hand-rolled any of it would grade itself, and the lane would report green
    over code no browser ever touched. test/e2e_lane_contract_test.rb asserts that
    render stays by name.

    THE PICKER IS NOT MOUNTED HERE, stated rather than left as a silent gap. Its
    canDeepLink gate reaches the answer through window.walletProvider.isMobile,
    which turf-monster ships and this gem does not; stubbing it would mean stubbing
    the very thing that decides, which is the lab grading itself again. That branch
    is browser-covered where it actually runs, in turf-monster's e2e/auth_modal.spec.js
    phone describe, which taps the row and decodes the payload. What is covered HERE
    is the half that lives in this gem: the deep link program itself.

    tweetnacl is deliberately NOT loaded. The gem partial solana_studio/deeplink_assets
    fetches it from a CDN and this lane never reaches offsite. Defining the entry point
    does not need nacl; only CALLING it does, so the spec that calls it stubs the two
    members that flow touches and drives the real shipped program for everything else.
%>
<% render_deeplink = params[:deeplink] == "1" %>

<%# The state marker, so a spec can prove it loaded the page it meant to rather
    than asserting against whatever document happened to be on screen. %>
<div data-test="deeplink-state" data-deeplink="<%= render_deeplink %>"></div>

<% if render_deeplink %>
  <%= render "solana_studio/phantom_deeplink" %>
<% end %>
